cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 'dh-provenance-journal: A provenance journal for registered research files
  and revision-specific decisions'
version: 0.1.0
type: software
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
license: MIT
abstract: A small provenance journal for registered research files, processing records,
  and revision-specific decisions in digital humanities projects, including interview
  material, transcripts, annotations, and data exports. Events are submitted through
  the provjournal command line or the provenance_journal Python API and appended to
  a journal with SHA-256 or HMAC-SHA-256 hash chaining. Decisions refer to one record,
  one artifact, and one file hash; changed bytes do not inherit an earlier approval.
  Verification checks the stored event chain and supported payloads. It does not discover
  unregistered material, prove that a processing step ran, establish personal identity,
  or certify a complete project history. Research files must be preserved separately.
  Python 3.11 or newer; standard library only at runtime. Command-line output is in
  German. The journal core derives from OHPIPE, as described in NOTICE.md.
authors:
- given-names: Klaus
  family-names: Behnam Shad
  orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3601-9024
  affiliation: Centre for Contemporary and Digital History (C2DH), Université du Luxembourg
repository-code: https://github.com/klausbehnamshad/dh-provenance-journal
keywords:
- provenance
- digital humanities
- oral history
- research data management
- hash chaining
- append-only journal
- decision log
